WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.970
What did we study in our last lesson?

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.490
We studied about meristematic tissues,
right?

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:16.210
Now tell me one thing, do plants also have
permanent tissues right when they

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.230
germinate from seeds?

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.189
Permanents tissues are composed of cells that
have

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:23.040
lost the power of dividing.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.030
That is kind of out of place, right?

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:31.460
The plant is growing and thus MUST have
only meristematic tissues.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.120
Permanent tissues would mean tissues that
are

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.910
already present and those that DO NOT divide.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.480
So initially if the plant does not
have PERMANENT tissues, where do they come

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.309
into the picture?

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:46.660
I am sure this is a mind-boggling question!

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.679
The answer is actually quite simple.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:54.350
When meristematic tissues have divided and
reached the final stage of

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.289
division, they attain maturity.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:00.780
After this point, these tissues do not divide
anymore.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.140
They only get differentiated into different
parts and these non-

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.360
dividing tissues then become PERMANENT tissues.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.360
Did you understand what
this means?

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.780
It means both the meristematic tissues and
permanent tissues are

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.520
one and the same.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.330
When tissues grow and divide, they are known
as

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.570
meristematic tissues.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.420
And when they finally mature and divide no
more, they

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.860
become permanent tissues.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:33.290
So permanent tissues are nothing but MATURED
meristematic tissues.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.770
Do you
know there are mainly two types of permanent

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.770
tissues?

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.500
Can you take a guess
at their names?

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.060
Yes, they are SIMPLE tissues and COMPLEX tissues.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.910
We will
look at the ‘simple permanent tissues’

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.880
in detail.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.320
The very word ‘SIMPLE’ means they have
very a simple structure.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.740
All the cells
of a simple permanent tissue are almost the

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.740
same.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:01.700
Do you know that there are
three subtypes of the simple permanent tissue?

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.560
Yes, and do you want to know
what they are called?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.420
PARENCHYMA, COLLENCHYMA and SCLERENCHYMA are
the three types of

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.920
simple permanent tissues.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.480
If you must know in one word what each of
these

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.780
tissues do, let us see what they can be called
otherwise.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.439
Parenchyma can be
called a ‘filler’ tissue; Collenchyma

00:02:23.439 --> 00:02:26.819
is a ‘supporter’ while sclerenchyma is
a

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:28.189
‘protector’ tissue.

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:31.840
We will look at each of these tissues in detail
in our coming videos.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.099
Stay tuned!

